# Line-ending policy (#143, 2026-08-17). Mirrors the #139 fix already in autoagent.
#
# Without `text=auto` the stored form of every file depends on each machine's local
# core.autocrlf setting, so the same file lands in the index as LF from one host and CRLF
# from another. Measured here before this file was written: index was 483 LF but ONE CRLF,
# and the worktree held 152 CRLF plus 40 genuinely MIXED files (both endings inside one
# file). Mixed files are the real damage -- they produce spurious whole-file diffs and
# make review noise indistinguishable from real change.
#
# `text=auto` means: normalise to LF in the repository, check out per-platform. Nothing
# below changes what a Windows editor sees in the worktree.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must be LF even on Windows checkouts -- CRLF breaks the shebang line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Ceremony-of-record files: preserve bytes exactly.
# orch_apply pre/post SHA-256 gates are computed on LF bytes; git CRLF normalization
# on checkout silently rewrites them and makes staged ceremonies fail their pre-sha
# check (this is exactly what invalidated the tier-hearth-note ceremony, 2026-07-03).
#
# NOTE (#143): this entry is why `* text=auto` above is safe. fleet_config.json is the
# ONE file whose index form is CRLF, and it is deliberate -- `-text` exempts it from
# renormalisation. Verified 2026-08-17: it is also the ONLY file in this repo carrying a
# git attribute, and the repo has NO POSTIMAGE/PREIMAGE/.diff ceremony files (autoagent's
# .gitattributes protects those; bifrost-router has none), so nothing else needs exempting.
# If byte-exact files are ever added here, give them `-text` BEFORE committing them.
fleet_config.json -text
